  id: Temporalis_muscle.R
  partName: Temporalis muscle R
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The temporalis is a large, fan-shaped muscle located on the side of the skull
    and is a major contributor to jaw closure. It elevates and retracts the mandible,
    allowing for powerful and controlled chewing. '
  - This muscle works alongside the masseter to provide the force needed for biting.
    It also plays a role in maintaining proper jaw alignment and ensuring smooth,
    coordinated movements during mastication and speech.
